Texture gamma bit 3 decodes alpha (TEXTURE_ADDRESS [23:20]), as RPCS3's _process_texel does.
Live draw decoded only the R/G/B bits of a unit's gamma field and kept alpha raw. RPCS3 [src:rpcs3-texops] reads the field in
R, G, B, A bit order and converts the whole texel with srgb_to_linear, masked per channel including GAMMA_A_MASK.
Tools of Destruction's environment cube (unit 7 of the scene shaders, A8R8G8B8 32x32, wrap 0x00F30303: gamma 0xF)
keeps an HDR exponent in alpha that the shaders apply as exp2(alpha * c3.x + c3.y): undecoded, the floors and other
reflective surfaces of Metropolis came out several times too bright (the "washed-out glow"; glow-cap1, first
Metropolis control frame, ground mean 193/190/142 against RPCS3's 71/69/48 at the same camera).
gamma_mask now holds 4 bits per unit (R, G, B, A; 16 units fill the u64), rsx_srgb takes a float4 mask and returns
the decoded channel where the mask is set and the fetched one elsewhere. LD_GAMMA_NO_ALPHA=1 = old R/G/B-only decode
(A/B). Host test: R&C port/rc/tests/run_gamma_alpha_test.sh.

